@title Your MRI Scan
@subtitle What to expect, from St. Anselm Imaging

!! Do you have a pacemaker, a cochlear implant, an aneurysm clip or any other metal implant? Call the imaging desk on extension 2210 at least 2 weeks before your scan. Some devices need special planning, and your scan may need to be rescheduled.

# Before the day

- If you have a metal implant, call the imaging desk on extension 2210 at least 2 weeks ahead.
- Tell us if you might be pregnant or have kidney disease.
- If you are uncomfortable in small spaces, ask your doctor about a mild sedative. Arrange a driver if you take one.
- If your scan uses contrast dye, do not eat for 4 hours before. You can still drink water.

# On the day

Arrive 30 minutes early at the Imaging Department on level 2.

Bring:

- [ ] A photo ID
- [ ] Your insurance details
- [ ] Your referral, if you were given a paper one

Leave jewelry, watches, hearing aids and wallets in the locker. Wear clothes without metal zippers or underwire.

# During the scan

kpi Scan time | 30 to 60 min | you lie on a padded bed | neutral

- The bed slides into a tube that is open at both ends.
- The machine is loud. We give you earplugs or headphones.
- You must keep very still.
- You hold a squeeze ball. Squeeze it at any moment to call the technologist.

# After the scan

- You can eat, drive and go back to work straight away, unless you took a sedative.
- Your doctor receives the results within 3 business days.
- Results appear in the patient portal after your doctor has seen them.
- If you had contrast, drink extra water.
